{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"f9f9ba73-819f-4682-8984-b998ae3a27f2","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/op-element/review-feedback-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[],"evidence":{"checked":29,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/export/permissions.test.ts","title":"generatePermissions tests still use free-token operation strings (by design)","rationale":"Per design decision D5, generatePermissions is a grammar-agnostic pure function. The existing makeGraph-based tests intentionally retain free-token operation strings ('create', 'list', etc.) to test the function independently of grammar. This is explicitly documented in tasks.md T-07. A comment citing D5 in the deterministic ordering describe block would help future maintainers, but it is not a defect."},{"severity":"low","file":"src/check/rules/op-element.test.ts","title":"TC-008 assertion uses OR that could theoretically match a different C6 error","rationale":"The assertion `d.message.includes('target') || d.message.includes('perm-deal')` is satisfied by the target constraint error. In practice the fixture has a valid operation line so the non-empty obligation error does not fire, making the test correctly exercised. Not a correctness bug; noted for maintainability awareness.","line":326}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-14T06:22:50.518Z","endedAt":"2026-08-14T06:31:00.157Z","commitOid":"7bf3bdaab921429aac988f45fc651b735fddae50"}
